From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Null IDE Build <build@nullide.local>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] feat: inject Null custom stylesheet into workbench HTML

Adds a <link> for null-custom.css after the main workbench stylesheet.
The source lives at workbench/custom.css in the overlay repo and is copied
to src/vs/workbench/browser/null-custom.css before the gulp build runs
(see "Copy workbench CSS" step in build.yml), so it ends up at
out/vs/workbench/null-custom.css in the packaged artifact.

The existing CSP already contains style-src 'self', so same-origin
stylesheets load without any policy change.

If a future VS Code version adds workbench.esm.html, apply the same
one-line change to that file as well.
---
 src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html b/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html
index a1b2c3d..e4f5a89 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 		<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; img-src 'self' https: data: blob: vscode-remote-resource: vscode-file:; media-src 'none'; child-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self' https: ws:; worker-src blob:; font-src 'self' https: blob:;">
 		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
 		<link data-name="vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main" rel="stylesheet" href="workbench.desktop.main.css">
+		<link rel="stylesheet" href="null-custom.css">
 	</head>
 	<body aria-label=""></body>
 </html>
